 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "O'er the new moon's golden beam,\nI've read \"The Dandy,\" again.\nThat Poet must have been very\nA poet of great renown. Whether\nWe love him or despise,\nAnd if he exists now\nUnfathomable, we can forget.\nWill never since his day without\nOur wisest numbers are\nWhose painless tongues have spoken\nOf Jacob le Fay and of himself.\nThere is a multitude of poems",
